# Two-button navigation (current hardware)

The unit has **only two physical buttons**. There is no on-device touch UI for settings today. SoftAP on a phone is the settings surface. Touch (CST816S swipe) is optional / future — **buttons remain the primary cabin input** until touch hardware is standard.

## Canonical map (`BUTTON_PIN` = GPIO0, `BUTTON_BOOT` = GPIO28)

| Input | Action | Timing |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GPIO0 short | Next page (or face primary short) | release before long |
| GPIO28 short | Previous page (or face secondary short) | — |
| GPIO0 long alone | SoftAP setup enter / leave | ~2 s (`kLongPressMs`) |
| Both held | Soft power-off → deep sleep | ~3 s (`kSoftOffHoldMs`) |
| GPIO0 after GPIO wake | Confirm stay awake | ~1.5 s (`kWakeConfirmMs`) |

Do not remap button roles when **Flip Display 180** is on — enclosure marks the setup button.

## Design constraints

- **No nested in-cabin menus** that need “select / back / adjust” with only two keys. Cabin = page cycle + SoftAP toggle + soft-off.
- **Settings and complex config** go to SoftAP (this face’s SSID on a phone), not a button-driven wizard on the cabin screen.
- When adding UI or features, answer: *how does the user reach / change this with two buttons?* If they cannot, put it on SoftAP or defer until touch.
- Prefer short-press for navigation, long-press / dual-hold for rare power/setup actions. Avoid new chord or timing schemes that collide with SoftAP (2 s) or soft-off (3 s both).
- Dual-hold soft-off must suppress SoftAP long-press.
- Soft-off blocked during OTA; SoftAP long-press unchanged while SoftAP is up (GPIO0 alone leaves).

## Future touch

Swipe can mirror next/previous when the touch IC is present. Do not remove or weaken button fallbacks. Until then, keep SoftAP as the apply/settings path.
